    "date": "2024-02-01",
    "content": "# Fine-tuning\n\nFine-tuning is the process of taking a pre-trained language model and further training it on a smaller, task-specific dataset. This allows the model to adapt its general knowledge to particular domains or use cases.\n\n## Why Fine-tune?\n\n1. **Domain Adaptation**: Specialize models for specific industries or topics\n2. **Task Optimization**: Improve performance on specific tasks\n3. **Style Transfer**: Adjust output style to match requirements\n4. **Cost Efficiency**: Smaller fine-tuned models can outperform larger general models\n\n## Fine-tuning Approaches\n\n### Full Fine-tuning\n\nUpdate all model parameters:\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer, TrainingArguments\nfrom trl import SFTTrainer\n\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\"meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B\")\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B\")\n\ntraining_args = TrainingArguments(\n    output_dir=\"./results\",\n    num_train_epochs=3,\n    per_device_train_batch_size=4,\n    learning_rate=2e-5,\n    weight_decay=0.01,\n)\n\ntrainer = SFTTrainer(\n    model=model,\n    args=training_args,\n    train_dataset=dataset,\n    tokenizer=tokenizer,\n)\n\ntrainer.train()\n```\n\n### LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation)\n\nEfficient fine-tuning by updating only low-rank matrices:\n\n```python\nfrom peft import LoraConfig, get_peft_model\n\nlora_config = LoraConfig(\n    r=16,  # rank\n    lora_alpha=32,\n    target_modules=[\"q_proj\", \"v_proj\", \"k_proj\", \"o_proj\"],\n    lora_dropout=0.05,\n    bias=\"none\",\n    task_type=\"CAUSAL_LM\"\n)\n\nmodel = get_peft_model(model, lora_config)\nmodel.print_trainable_parameters()\n# trainable params: 13,631,488 || all params: 8,040,346,624 || trainable%: 0.17\n```\n\n### QLoRA (Quantized LoRA)\n\nFine-tune quantized models for memory-constrained environments:\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import BitsAndBytesConfig\nimport torch\n\nbnb_config = BitsAndBytesConfig(\n    load_in_4bit=True,\n    bnb_4bit_quant_type=\"nf4\",\n    bnb_4bit_compute_dtype=torch.float16,\n    bnb_4bit_use_double_quant=True,\n)\n\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n    \"meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B\",\n    quantization_config=bnb_config,\n    device_map=\"auto\"\n)\n```\n\n## Data Preparation\n\n### Format Data\n\nPrepare training data in the correct format:\n\n```python\n# Chat format\ndef format_conversation(example):\n    messages = [\n        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": example[\"system\"]},\n        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": example[\"question\"]},\n        {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": example[\"answer\"]}\n    ]\n    return {\"text\": tokenizer.apply_chat_template(messages, tokenize=False)}\n```\n\n### Quality Data\n\nKey principles for fine-tuning data:\n\n1. **Consistency**: Ensure consistent formatting and style\n2. **Diversity**: Cover various scenarios and edge cases\n3. **Accuracy**: Verify correctness of training examples\n4. **Volume**: Typically 1,000-100,000 examples depending on task\n\n## Evaluation\n\nMonitor training progress:\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import EvaluationStrategy\n\ntraining_args = TrainingArguments(\n    evaluation_strategy=\"steps\",\n    eval_steps=100,\n    load_best_model_at_end=True,\n    metric_for_best_model=\"eval_loss\",\n)\n```\n\n## Common Challenges\n\n### Overfitting\n\nWhen the model memorizes training data:\n\n- Use dropout and weight decay\n- Early stopping\n- Data augmentation\n- Reduce model capacity\n\n### Catastrophic Forgetting\n\nWhen the model loses general capabilities:\n\n- Use lower learning rates\n- Regularization techniques\n- Mix general and task-specific data\n\n### Hallucination\n\nWhen the model generates incorrect information:\n\n- Ground responses in provided context\n- Use retrieval-augmented generation\n- Validate against known facts\n\n## Tools and Frameworks\n\n- **Hugging Face TRL**: Transformer Reinforcement Learning\n- **Axolotl**: Fine-tuning framework\n- **LLaMA-Factory**: All-in-one fine-tuning solution\n- **Unsloth**: Fast fine-tuning with quantization",
