    "date": "2024-04-01",
    "content": "# Ollama\n\nOllama is a tool that allows you to run large language models locally on your machine. It simplifies the process of downloading, setting up, and running LLMs with a simple CLI interface.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Simple CLI**: Run models with single commands\n- **Local Inference**: No internet connection required after download\n- **Model Library**: Access to popular open-source models\n- **Quantization**: Efficient model compression for consumer hardware\n- **API Server**: OpenAI-compatible API for integration\n\n## Getting Started\n\n### Installation\n\n```bash\n# macOS\nbrew install ollama\n\n# Linux\ncurl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\n\n# Windows\n# Download from https://ollama.com/download\n```\n\n### Running Models\n\n```bash\n# Download and run a model\nollama run llama3.1\n\n# Run a specific version\nollama run llama3.1:70b\n\n# List available models\nollama list\n\n# Pull a model without running\nollama pull mistral\n```\n\n## Model Library\n\nOllama supports many popular models:\n\n| Model | Parameters | Best For |\n|-------|-----------|----------|\n| Llama 3.1 | 8B, 70B, 405B | General purpose |\n| Mistral | 7B | Fast inference |\n| Code Llama | 7B, 13B, 70B | Code generation |\n| Phi-3 | 3.8B, 14B | Small but capable |\n| Gemma | 2B, 7B | Google's models |\n\n## API Usage\n\nOllama provides an OpenAI-compatible API:\n\n```python\nimport openai\n\nclient = openai.OpenAI(\n    base_url=\"http://localhost:11434/v1\",\n    api_key=\"ollama\"\n)\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=\"llama3.1\",\n    messages=[\n        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"}\n    ]\n)\n```\n\n## Custom Models\n\nCreate custom models with Modelfiles:\n\n```dockerfile\n# Modelfile\nFROM llama3.1\n\nSYSTEM \"You are a helpful coding assistant.\"\n\nPARAMETER temperature 0.7\nPARAMETER num_ctx 4096\n```\n\n```bash\n# Create custom model\nollama create coding-assistant -f Modelfile\n```\n\n## Use Cases\n\n- **Development**: Test models locally before deployment\n- **Privacy**: Keep sensitive data on your machine\n- **Offline**: Use AI without internet connection\n- **Learning**: Experiment with different models\n- **Edge Deployment**: Run models on edge devices",
